        "correct. This confirms Member 1's earlier finding: **the missingness in `avg_order_value_kes` is\n",
        "random/non-structural, not structural.**\n",
        "\n",
        "Because it is random, we treat it with **statistical imputation** rather than a domain fill. Given\n",
        "the right-skewed distribution Member 1 documented for this feature (Section 1.8), the median\n",
        "is used rather than the mean, since the median is not pulled toward the small number of very high\n",
        "average-order-value customers. We use `sklearn`'s `SimpleImputer` (rather than `.fillna()`\n",
        "directly) specifically because a fitted imputer object like the scaler can be saved and\n",
        "re-applied identically to new, unseen customers later."
      ]
