      "source": [
        "### 3.5 Keeping the Fitted Scaler (and Imputer) for reuse on new customers\n",
        "\n",
        "Before a new, unseen customer can be assigned to a cluster with the final fitted K-Means model, that customer's raw data must go through the exact same imputation and scaling used here not a freshly fit imputer/scaler. Re-fitting on new data (even a single new customer) would compute a different median, mean, and standard deviation, and silently distort every distance calculation against the trained cluster centroids.\n",
        "\n",
        "For that reason, the fitted `imputer` and `scaler` objects above are kept as live Python variables for the rest of this notebook, and are also persisted to disk with `joblib` so they survive independently of notebook re-runs and can be reloaded later for scoring new customers.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
