    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d8bb25b6",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 4.5 Compare the 3 methods\n",
        "The three methods are now compared directly:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Elbow Method:** identifies where the reduction in inertia begins to level off.\n",
        "- **Silhouette Score:** higher values indicate better-separated and more cohesive clusters.\n",
        "- **Davies-Bouldin Index:** lower values indicate more compact and well-separated clusters.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because the elbow is based on the shape of the inertia curve rather than simply taking a minimum or maximum value, we estimate the elbow point using `KneeLocator`.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 877,
      "id": "f4b605f5",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
