    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "746189a1",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Scaling Robustness Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "`StandardScaler` was used in the main analysis because it places all four customer-behavior variables on comparable standardized scales. As a robustness check, the clustering analysis was repeated using `RobustScaler`, which is less influenced by extreme values because it uses the median and interquartile range.\n",
        "\n",
        "The purpose of this test is not automatically to replace the StandardScaler model. Instead, it checks whether the preferred number of customer segments depends heavily on the scaling method.\n",
        "\n",
        "If StandardScaler and RobustScaler identify the same or nearby values of `k`, this strengthens confidence that the customer segmentation structure is reasonably robust. If they identify substantially different values, scaling choice materially affects the clustering solution and should be considered when Member 5 selects the final `k`."
      ]
    },
